      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The risk of developing post-herpetic neuralgia is related to the degree of residual scarring. Subjects over the age of 60 with more than 10 cm2 of residual scarring have a very high risk of developing intractable post-herpetic neuralgia. Left-handed subjects are less likely to develop herpes zoster, and this could be due to a more efficient immune system."},
